The **Attention Mechanism** (30:19) is a foundational concept that 
allows Large Language Models (LLMs) to understand the **contextual 
meaning** of words based on their relationship to other words in a 
sentence.

### Why Attention Matters

Simply converting words into vector embeddings isn't enough 
because words can have different meanings based on the context.   
For example, in the sentences "I code in Python" and "A Python bit me," 
the word "Python" refers to two entirely different things: 
a **programming language** and a **snake**. The Attention Mechanism 
helps the model determine which other words in the sentence provide 
the necessary context to clarify the meaning.

